# Security and privacy

This platform does not take payments and does not collect card data. Do not add a payment provider,
a card form, or checkout.

## GDPR / privacy
- Privacy by default: `social_feed_enabled` defaults off. Creating a post or a comment requires that flag
  (database-enforced) plus an explicit action. Audience defaults to the stricter choice the user picked;
  do not silently publish as public.
- Lawful basis per data use. Marketing pushes and analytics SDKs need consent recorded in `user_consents`
  (append-only; check with `UserConsent::isGranted()`). Transactional notifications (a comment on your
  reel, a follow request) do not.
- Data minimization: no date of birth, no contacts upload unless `contacts_matching` consent (hash phone
  numbers and emails on the device before upload), no raw IP or user agent (store HMAC hashes only).
- Never query by an encrypted column. Device fingerprints use HMAC with `FINGERPRINT_PEPPER`.
- Serialization: `User` exposes only id, username, display_name, avatar_path by default. Any other field
  goes through an explicit API Resource checked by a policy. Never expose email, devices, consents, or
  `risk_status` to other users. Never expose who liked a post.
- Right of access (Art. 15/20): export the user, consents, devices (without push tokens), posts, comments,
  likes, and connections.
- Right to erasure (Art. 17): `anonymize_user()` after the grace period, then purge that user's media from
  object storage and the CDN, plus search indexes and analytics. The user row is scrubbed, not deleted.
- Retention: purge `inbound_webhooks.payload` after 90 days.
- Logs and monitoring: no PII, no tokens, no full URLs with query strings.
- Processors (object storage, CDN, Expo push, email, analytics, hosting) need DPAs; send them the minimum.

## Authorization
- Every model a user can mutate has a Policy; controllers call `authorize()` or `can` middleware.
- Load owned resources through the authenticated user (`$request->user()->posts()->findOrFail($id)`).
  A feed read of someone else's reel still goes through `visibleTo` and the block filter.
- Sanctum tokens per device with abilities; revoke on logout and when a device is revoked.
- Rate-limit auth, OTP, follow requests, post creation, likes, comments, shares, and webhooks.
- Admin actions use a separate guard and 2FA.

## Abuse
- Velocity checks on posts, comments, likes, follows, and new accounts from the same
  `device_fingerprint_hash`. Set `users.risk_status` to `review` or `restricted` when a limit is exceeded.
  Restricted users cannot post, comment, or follow.
- Webhooks: verify signatures or allow-listed sources, store the event first, process it idempotently.
- Uploads are re-encoded before they are stored. Reject anything that is not an allowed image or video type.
